---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Submission Guidelines - CICON Hack 2025";
const description = "How to prepare and submit your project for CICON Hack 2025.";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <main>
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-content">
          <div class="hero-title-container">
            <h1 class="hero-title">Submission Guidelines</h1>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-description">
            Everything you need to know to prepare your project submission for CICON Hack 2025.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Guidelines Section -->
    <section class="guidelines-section">
      <div class="container">
        <p>
          Please prepare a short presentation answering the points below. We do not need a prototype for this phase—we just want to understand your idea first. A clear presentation helps us evaluate every project fairly.
        </p>

        <ol class="guidelines-list">
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Team Name</strong></h3>
            <p>Pick a name that can be used publicly. Keep it respectful and appropriate for a public event.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Team Members</strong></h3>
            <p>List the names of everyone in your team.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Roles</strong></h3>
            <p>Briefly describe what each person is contributing to the project. For example: design, research, frontend, backend, writing, video editing, etc.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Your Idea</strong></h3>
            <p>Please explain your idea using the following structure:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Problem Statement</strong>: What issue are you trying to solve?</li>
              <li><strong>Proposed Solution</strong>: What are you building and how does it help?</li>
              <li><strong>Expected Impact and Benefits</strong>: Who will benefit and in what way?</li>
              <li><strong>Resource Requirements</strong>: What do you need to make this work? (tools, time, people, etc.)</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>How It Fits the Hackathon Theme</strong></h3>
            <p>
              How does your idea connect to the themes of this hackathon? (e.g. community repair, small shop automation, repair content creation, etc.)
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Why This Idea Matters</strong></h3>
            <p>
              Why do you think this is worth building? Have you noticed this problem in your own life, online, or in your community?
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Similar Ideas</strong></h3>
            <p>
              Have you seen any projects or products that are somewhat similar? What makes yours different or more focused on repair or impact?
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Tech Stack or Tools (if any)</strong></h3>
            <p>
              List any tools, languages, or platforms you plan to use. If you’re not building something technical, you can skip this.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>How Your Project Works</strong></h3>
            <p>Use diagrams or short explanations to show how your project is structured. If applicable, include:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>What are the main parts of the project?</li>
              <li>How do these parts connect or work together?</li>
              <li>What tools or platforms will be used for each part?</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3><strong>Anything Else You Want to Share?</strong></h3>
            <p>
              Use this space to mention anything we haven’t asked. For example: what inspired you, early sketches, extra ideas, or what you hope to do next.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="submission-note">
          <p>
            <strong>Submissions are not open yet.</strong> They will open after registration closes on <strong>17 Aug 2025 at 11:59&nbsp;PM GMT+7</strong>.
            The submission window will run from <strong>18 Aug to 25 Aug 2025 at 11:59&nbsp;PM GMT+7</strong>. If you have any questions, please feel free to send us an email or ask on Discord&nbsp;😃
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
